113 questions about evolution with John  Perry hanging out with cousin Paige  Malibu Edition how old should a person  be before learning about evolution  this is kind of a question about  parenting so different parents would  have different opinions about this but  evolution is about reproduction and  death really  you know there's survival and  reproduction and so for someone to  really understand really dig into  evolution and understand it inside and  out they need to understand they need to  be old enough to understand what  reproduction is and what death is so for  different kids that come at different  times  I suppose you know I'd say maybe a lot  of kids could learn about that when  they're about eight between eight to ten  but there are simpler parts of evolution  more friendlier parts I guess you could  say that kids are ready to learn when a  lot younger like kids can learn that  they're related to other animals you  know there's a there's a really good  book called grandmother fish which is  for little kids and it just talks about  the relationship that we have between us  and other animals and you could you can  start teaching kids that when they're  you know as soon as they can talk and  point at animals as soon as they notice  that animals are different than them you  can point out similarities and  differences for me when I was a little  cats probably five when I noticed that I  was the same as my dog we had the same  bones and I noticed that his his back  legs it looked like he had backwards  knees but I realized it's actually his  heel bone was a little backwards neat  looking thing and I got super excited  and told my parents all about it and  kids can start to learn that they're  related to plants and animals and all  other organisms as soon as they start to  learn about organisms but I would say  before you really really dig into the  details of evolution you need to  understand what reproduction is and what  death is  you
 

